# Session screenshots keep landing in the repo root — never track them.
/*.png

# graphify knowledge graph. graph.json is ~14MB and rewritten whole on every
# rebuild, so git cannot delta it — committing it would grow .git by that much
# per run. All of it is derived from the source tree except cache/semantic/,
# which holds the LLM doc extraction (~400k tokens to regenerate) as one
# content-hashed file per doc; that IS tracked, so a fresh clone rebuilds free
# and an edited doc adds one small blob instead of rewriting the set.
#
# cache/stat-index.json stays ignored — it records machine-local mtime_ns and
# would conflict on every machine.
#
# The `dir/*` + `!dir/sub/` shape is required: git will not descend into a
# directory excluded as `dir/`, so a negation inside it can never match.
# graphify writes its output next to whatever path it was pointed at, so both
# the repo-root and apps/ scopes are covered.
graphify-out/*
!graphify-out/cache/
graphify-out/cache/*
!graphify-out/cache/semantic/
apps/graphify-out/*
!apps/graphify-out/cache/
apps/graphify-out/cache/*
!apps/graphify-out/cache/semantic/
